# secrets
.env

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# local Wikidata API cache (regenerable, can be large)
tkg_cache*.db

# dry-run / checkpoint test outputs (test_dryrun.py)
dryrun_results.jsonl
dryrun_checkpoint_test.jsonl

# archived / intermediate snapshots from past exposure-mechanism iterations and
# one-off relabel passes — debug history, not the canonical current results.
# results.jsonl / summary.csv / summary_conflict_vs_control.csv (no suffix) ARE
# tracked intentionally: they're this pilot's current output, kept for reviewer
# transparency rather than treated as disposable build artifacts.
results_legacy_v1.jsonl
results_prerelabel_backup*.jsonl
results_prerelabel_final.jsonl
results_v2_*.jsonl
results_v3_*.jsonl
results_relabeled*.jsonl
summary_v2_*.csv
summary_v3_*.csv
summary_conflict_vs_control_v2_*.csv
summary_conflict_vs_control_v3_*.csv

# same convention for 選項 B (results_free_exploration.jsonl / hit_rate_by_distance.csv
# with no suffix are the current canonical output — this is the first run, before the
# Line B transition + PK probe fixes, so conflict-arm ripple answers are all bogus
# ("other" — the model was stuck asking to re-use exploration tools that no longer
# existed) and there's no PK-probe kill-gate data at all
results_free_exploration_v1_*.jsonl
hit_rate_by_distance_v1_*.csv
# v2: transition prompt fixed the "let me use a tool" confusion, but its wording
# ("根據你目前已知的資訊") got misread as "graph-observed facts only", so the
# model refused to answer using its own general knowledge — still bogus data
results_free_exploration_v2_*.jsonl
hit_rate_by_distance_v2_*.csv
# v3: n=1 sanity check after the general-knowledge fix, happened to miss (model
# didn't move) — just variance, not a bug, but not enough data to be useful either
results_free_exploration_v3_*.jsonl
hit_rate_by_distance_v3_*.csv
# v4: general-knowledge fix worked, but discovered "hit" (move_to reached pivot_qid)
# didn't mean the model ever actually viewed the pivot's facts — move_to only
# confirmed movement, exposure never happened. Fixed: move_to now auto-reveals the
# destination's facts (like clicking a real wiki link shows the page content)
results_free_exploration_v4_*.jsonl
hit_rate_by_distance_v4_*.csv
# v5: exposure now real, but Apple Inc.'s 1160-fact node meant the CEO claim was
# truncated out of the top-30 shown facts entirely — fixed by prioritizing
# time-qualified (dynamic) claims over static ones when rendering. Also found the
# missing-label fallback (for John Ternus's unlabeled Wikidata stub) leaked the
# distance-1 "prior role" ripple answer via its description text — fixed by
# dropping that one ripple candidate from apple_ceo (see cases.json _distance1_note)
results_free_exploration_v5_*.jsonl
hit_rate_by_distance_v5_*.csv
